# Written by an executor for Q20 (collab/QUESTIONS.md); the documenter may edit or drop it.
# Story: an ordinary desk, as it stood on the first day played with real apps on a hosted Mac: a display 1600 points wide, Finder,
# Safari and TextEdit to be docked, and Terminal, Notes, Calendar and Mail floating where their person left them. On that day a
# dock squeezed Safari from 1324 to 794 points, and ⌘M, ⌘H and ⌘Q of a docked window shoved the others about.
# Arbor sets a floating window's frame only to take it out of view and to put it back exactly where it was.
# Reference: rules 2, 3 and 5 of the product direction.
display-size 1600x822 31
open Finder 920x436 min 501x200
open Safari 1324x791 min 574x200
open TextEdit 673x439 min 252x200
open Terminal 877x499 min 240x200
open Notes 1000x660 min 709x200
open Calendar 935x598 min 680x200
open Mail 1120x630 min 871x200
move 102 138 31 1324 791
move 103 165 65 673 439
move 104 40 51 877 499
move 105 300 105 1000 660
move 106 200 86 935 598
move 107 240 72 1120 630
# The first dock. Nobody else moves, and nobody is made smaller.
dock 101 left
expect at 102 138 31 1324x791
expect at 103 165 65 673x439
expect at 104 40 51 877x499
expect at 105 300 105 1000x660
expect at 106 200 86 935x598
expect at 107 240 72 1120x630
expect focused 101
dock 102 right
dock 103 right
expect at 104 40 51 877x499
expect at 105 300 105 1000x660
expect at 106 200 86 935x598
expect at 107 240 72 1120x630
# Frame, then Show Everything: there and back is nothing.
zoom 102
expect hidden 104
expect hidden 105
expect hidden 106
expect hidden 107
show-all
expect at 104 40 51 877x499
expect at 105 300 105 1000x660
expect at 106 200 86 935x598
expect at 107 240 72 1120x630
# ⌘M in Safari, and back out of the Dock.
minimize 102
expect at 104 40 51 877x499
expect at 105 300 105 1000x660
restore 102
expect at 104 40 51 877x499
expect at 105 300 105 1000x660
# ⌘H in Finder, and back.
hide Finder
flush
expect at 104 40 51 877x499
expect at 107 240 72 1120x630
unhide Finder
flush
expect at 104 40 51 877x499
expect at 107 240 72 1120x630
# ⌘Q in TextEdit.
close 103
expect at 104 40 51 877x499
expect at 105 300 105 1000x660
expect at 106 200 86 935x598
expect at 107 240 72 1120x630
# Left hanging over the edge of the screen and over Finder by hand, it comes back to that.
move 105 -300 200 1000 560
zoom 102
show-all
expect at 105 -300 200 1000x560
# ⌃⌥D shows all that floats.
desktop
expect camera desktop
expect at 104 40 51 877x499
expect at 105 -300 200 1000x560
back
# Whoever liked it better before can have it back: the next time the Desktop comes into view its windows are gathered on it. Finder and
# Safari have left it no room (F68), and where there is none there is nowhere to gather them: Safari floats, and what it had is left over.
set floatingWindowsMakeWay true
float 102
zoom 101
show-all
expect left-of 101 104
